[ ] Lint the minimal CLI profile in CI =lint-minimal $Found 2026-10-06: cargo build --release -p clearhead --no-default-features warns dead_code, and CI lints only default features, so the minimal profile drifts unseen. Add a clippy step with --no-default-features (-D warnings), then fix what it finds.$ !4 ^2026-10-06T10:41 #01a1124e-2a1c-74fe-ae3e-14f6701598ca
[ ] Test the CLI on Windows in CI =windows-ci $Decided 2026-10-06: before a Windows binary, prove the suite on a windows-latest runner. A Windows build is then one target in dist-workspace.toml (x86_64-pc-windows-msvc; ARM Windows runs it under emulation). Checked from Linux: no Unix-only dependencies, app:file paths are joined with /, and a CRLF .actions file lints exactly as LF. Unknown until it runs: the test suite, and atomic replace while an editor holds the file.$ !4 ^2026-10-06T15:09 #01a11343-bb68-7361-9d1c-75244453feb0
[ ] Keep line endings when formatting .actions =keep-line-endings $Found 2026-10-06: format file rewrites a CRLF .actions file with LF, while charters keep the line ending they were written with. Pick one rule for every file the CLI writes, and say it in the specification.$ !4 ^2026-10-06T15:09 #01a11343-bb79-749d-938c-8989d16bab59
[ ] One changelog format\: Keep a Changelog =changelog-format $Decided with the human 2026-10-06: each project keeps its own changelog; roots are assembled from them by a script, never edited. Assembly extracts a version section with parse-changelog (the parser dist uses), which takes a section to end at the next ## heading, so entries must live under their version: Unreleased, renamed to x.y.z - date at release. The grammar and Core already do this; convert the specification (its v0.2.0 em-dash heading is not found) and the CLI (its 0.3.0 section excludes the dated entries below it), give clearhead.nvim a changelog, bring Core past 0.1.0, and move the CLI Roadmap section to a charter if still live.$ !4 ^2026-10-06T15:50 #01a11369-8cb1-731d-acdd-02ac93a2e67d
[ ] Assemble clearhead-core's root changelog =core-root-changelog $A script assembles the root CHANGELOG.md from Core's and the CLI's, committed because dist reads its release notes only from a real root file; CI regenerates it and fails on a difference. Then regenerate the v0.3.0 release notes, which shipped with none.$ !4 ^2026-10-06T15:50 <changelog-format #01a11369-8cc5-7639-91fe-4ba6541b1cea
[ ] Release the platform as a set of pinned components =platform-release $A platform release tags the platform repository whose gitlinks are component releases; proposed CalVer (2026.10.0), since the bundle has no single notion of breaking. Its changelog is assembled per release: for each component whose pin moved, that component's sections between the old and new versions, read from git.$ !5 ^2026-10-06T15:50 <core-root-changelog #01a11369-8cd7-76c0-83fa-6fd49112f05b
